# THE DEMANDS FILED AS A RANGE. One row per layer whose demand spans a width, so there is
# something a narrowing statement could actually reduce.
#
# ⭐⭐ THIS IS THE DENOMINATOR FOR THE ONE NUMBER A RECEIVER IS ENTITLED TO STATE AS A FACT.
#    Judging whether a narrowing sentence WOULD narrow the range is prose and belongs to a
#    person. Counting how many ranges decline to say anything at all is arithmetic, and it
#    turns "a claim without one is weaker" from an opinion into a figure.
#
# ⛔ AND THE MIRROR OF THE POINT-VALUE RULE LIVES HERE: a range that files `narrowsWhen` as
#   `notApplicable` is claiming it has no range, in a row that demonstrably has one.
-- pm:Claim on pm:Demand where low <> high.
SELECT d.*
FROM (
    :compose(layers/demand.sqlc)
) d
WHERE NOT d.is_a_point
